    title: "Bakeoff init should default to new session, not reuse existing — prevents accidental data destruction"  # 4fe5
    status: todo_hard  # 4fe5
    priority: 1  # 4fe5
    parent:  # 4fe5
    tags: []  # 4fe5
    before: []  # 4fe5
    duplicate_of: []  # 4fe5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 4fe5
    pr_ref:  # 4fe5
    description: "When bakeoff-features init is called with the same pool, it silently reuses the existing session. This led to rm -rf of completed bakeoff outputs when trying to re-run with code fixes. Fixes needed: (1) init should create a new timestamped session by default, not reuse; (2) add --resume flag for explicit reuse; (3) when reusing, warn about existing outputs and suggest safe alternatives; (4) run --all should refuse to overwrite without --force."  # 4fe5
    fields: {}  # 4fe5
